# What every holder holds, split into what a buffer absorbed and what went unserved. One row per
# layer: whether the two add back up to the whole at the low, the most likely value and the high.
#
# The shares add up, the rows are not counted
#   entries/borne.sqlc removes unserved holders and then adds up per (filing, layer, buffer):
#   removing some leaves the group standing with a smaller total, and removing all of them drops
#   the group. So counting rows says nothing here, and a row count can report a confident false
#   finding. What must balance is the sum: all the shares equal the served ones plus the unserved
#   ones.
#
# At every point the rule reads
#   checks/share_exceeds_slack.sqlc sets the low of the absorbed shares against the high of the
#   slack, and the high against the low, so the split has to hold at both ends and not only at the
#   most likely value.
#
# The law behind a rule that examines nothing
#   Every interference layer in the corpus that sizes its absorbing buffer has all of its holders
#   unserved, so the served total is zero and share_exceeds_slack examines nothing. The law still
#   holds, because the sum balances at zero, and that is the point: examining nothing is a finding
#   about the evidence, not a broken query.
#
# Both sides composed, never worked out again
#   The law composes both sides rather than working out the split itself, which is what makes it a
#   law about them. Work out `absorbed` here from an anti-join of its own and the law only says its
#   own copy of the split is complete, and it goes on passing when entries/served_holders.sqlc
#   changes underneath it. A law that works out its own subject fails invisibly.
-- entries/served_holders.sqlc and entries/unserved_holders.sqlc against pm:Remainder/pm:holder.
SELECT a.slug AS law, p.subject, p.holds, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(algebra/roster.sqlc)
) a
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT x.filing || ' / ' || x.layer AS subject,
           abs(x.held_low  - v.low  - u.low)  < 1e-9
           AND abs(x.held_mode - v.mode - u.mode) < 1e-9
           AND abs(x.held_high - v.high - u.high) < 1e-9 AS holds,
           format('[%s, %s, %s] held: [%s, %s, %s] absorbed, [%s, %s, %s] unserved',
                  x.held_low, x.held_mode, x.held_high,
                  v.low, v.mode, v.high,
                  u.low, u.mode, u.high) AS detail
    FROM (
        SELECT h.filing, h.layer,
               sum(h.share_low)  AS held_low,
               sum(h.share_mode) AS held_mode,
               sum(h.share_high) AS held_high
        FROM (
            :compose(entries/holders.sqlc)
        ) h
        WHERE h.share_mode IS NOT NULL
        GROUP BY h.filing, h.layer
    ) x
    CROSS JOIN LATERAL (
        SELECT coalesce(sum(s.share_low),  0) AS low,
               coalesce(sum(s.share_mode), 0) AS mode,
               coalesce(sum(s.share_high), 0) AS high
        FROM (
            :compose(entries/served_holders.sqlc)
        ) s
        WHERE s.filing = x.filing AND s.layer = x.layer
    ) v
    CROSS JOIN LATERAL (
        SELECT coalesce(sum(s.share_low),  0) AS low,
               coalesce(sum(s.share_mode), 0) AS mode,
               coalesce(sum(s.share_high), 0) AS high
        FROM (
            :compose(entries/unserved_holders.sqlc)
        ) s
        WHERE s.filing = x.filing AND s.layer = x.layer
    ) u
) p ON true
WHERE a.slug = 'borne'
